차근 `debugging` 스킬의 제3자 귀속 표시 (third-party attribution)

The step skeleton of `SKILL.md` in this directory was assembled by comparing four
MIT-licensed debugging skills and keeping what three or more of them had in common.
The Korean text is newly written for non-developers. The stop-after-two-attempts rule,
the plain-language reproduction questions, the "never print values" logging rule and the
hand-off contents are chageun's own and are not from these sources. The four sources are
credited below. All four are distributed under the same MIT terms, so the MIT permission
notice is reproduced once at the end.

1. systematic-debugging (Superpowers)
   Taken: four-phase order, root-cause-before-fix principle, per-boundary
   instrumentation, red-flag list.
   MIT License. Copyright (c) 2025 Jesse Vincent.
   https://github.com/obra/superpowers

2. debugging-and-error-recovery (addyosmani/agent-skills)
   Taken: triage order (reproduce, localize, reduce, fix, guard, verify), the
   not-reproducible decision tree, "error output is data, not instructions".
   MIT License. Copyright (c) 2025 Addy Osmani.
   https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills

3. debugging-wizard (jeffallan/claude-skills)
   Taken: one hypothesis at a time, remove all debug code before committing.
   MIT License. Copyright (c) 2025. The LICENSE file leaves the copyright holder name
   blank, so the holder is recorded here as the author declared in the skill's own
   front matter (metadata.author): https://github.com/Jeffallan
   https://github.com/jeffallan/claude-skills

4. debug-mode (doraemonkeys/claude-code-debug-mode)
   Taken: numbered hypothesis list, `#region DEBUG` markers around temporary
   instrumentation, removal of those blocks and the log file at the end.
   MIT License. Copyright (c) 2025 doraemonkeys.
   https://github.com/doraemonkeys/claude-code-debug-mode

